===persian===

وقتی دلتنگم به تو می‌اندیشم
یاد تو مربعی‌ست محو و لرزان
در زمینه خاکستری روشن
در این مربع‌ها
من
با بهم زدن پلک‌هایم
گذشته را نقاشی می‌کنم.
بین من و تو
غبار و دیوار است
به سحر این مربع‌ها
من از دیوارها می‌گذرم
در رسیدن به تو
تنها راه گذشتن است
باید چراغ رنگ بدست بگیرم
و در خاکستری‌هایم به دنبال تو بگردم
ای کاش می‌توانستم
یک قطره بیشتر
با سرخ نقاشی کنم...

تهران ۱۳۶۸

===machine===

When I am homesick, I think of you
The memory of you is a faded, trembling square
On a light gray background
In these squares
I
By blinking my eyelids
Paint the past.
Between you and me
There is dust and a wall
By the magic of these squares
I pass through the walls
In reaching you
The only way is to pass
I must take up the lantern of color
And search for you in my grays
I wish I could
Paint one drop more
With red...

Tehran 1368

===lantern===

When the longing takes me, I think of you.
The memory of you is a square, blurred and trembling
against a ground of pale grey.
Inside these squares
I —
with the shutting of my eyelids —
paint the past.
Between you and me
there is dust, and a wall.
By the magic of these squares
I pass through the walls;
to reach you,
the only road is through.
I must take up the lamp of colour
and go looking for you in my greys.
If only I could lay down
one more drop
of red...

— Tehran, 1368

===translation===

===footnotes===

A painter's poem — Jafari was a painter as well as a poet, and it shows: memory as a blurred square on a grey ground, the eyelids' blink as a brushstroke, grief held in a palette drained to grey, with red the one withheld colour of life and love. چراغ رنگ is literally "the lamp/lantern of colour"; the machine pass already reached for "lantern," which sits oddly close to this collection's own name for the working-draft layer, so the finished line keeps "lamp." سحر here is سِحر (magic, enchantment), not سحَر (dawn).
